# detail
Number of changes: 1

1. Modified | Function implementation code block
   Replaced the body of `is_safe_url`.
   The original implementation included:

   * Conditional statement: call `strip()` when `url` was not `None`;
   * Conditional statement: return `False` when `url` was empty;
   * Conditional statements: set `allowed_hosts` to `set()` when it was `None`, and convert it to a set when it was a string;
   * Return statement: call `_is_safe_url()` for the original `url` and for `url` with backslashes replaced, and return the logical conjunction of the two results.

   The new implementation includes:

   * API call: call `warnings.warn()` to issue `RemovedInDjango40Warning`;
   * Return statement: call and return `url_has_allowed_host_and_scheme(url, allowed_hosts, require_https)`.
# /detail
